# led_proc_init.soc  —  Ciena 8140 (Rudra40 / Jericho2C+ / BCM8885X)
#
# Loads the Broadcom M0 "custom LED" microcode so the ASIC shifts out the
# per-port LED serial frame (link + activity -> on/off/blink).  The Rudra40
# FPGA supplies the per-port COLOUR from its LED rate registers and combines
# it with this frame to drive the physical RGB LEDs (sfp/qsfpColourViaFpga).
#
# This file is auto-executed by docker-syncd-brcm-dnx/start_led.sh, which runs
#   bcmcmd -t 60 "rcload /usr/share/sonic/platform/led_proc_init.soc"
# after syncd/SDK is ready (and NOT during warmboot).
#
# NOTE (hardware validation): the exact DNX/M0SSQ LED command form was confirmed
# on hardware: `led 0 load <file>` requires an ASCII-hex file (one 2-digit hex
# byte per line)
# The SDK loads the default linkscan LED firmware automatically at init;
# m0 load 0 0x0 /usr/share/sonic/platform/linkscan_led_fw.bin

led 0 stop
led 0 load /usr/share/sonic/platform/CN8140CustomLed.hex
led 0 auto on
led 0 start
led status
